MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This can happen occasionally.  The min.width argument specifies the minimum number of probes in the minor arc of the circular (remember this is circular binary segmentation).  So if you can get 2 probes from one end and 3 from the other to be significantly different the middle you will get a significant result and a segmentation.  I need to change the code in order to eliminate this possibility.

Venkat

